.sp
.in 19n
.ti 0n
Viewing files    ：pager\*[usilic-tab]
.in 0
.sp
.in 8n
When started with file arguments ("usilic file"^M) or through standard input without arguments ("usilic < file"^M etc.), usilic(1) works as a pager for viewing files. When started with several file arguments, n/p move to the next/previous file, x/f to the first/last file, and q quits.
.br
.sp
After startup, usilic(1) shows a status line like the one below (mode-line below) on the bottom line of the screen.
.in 0
.sp
.in 12n
 /\*[usilic-i]Users\*[usilic-ie]/\*[usilic-i]usilic\*[usilic-ie]/\*[usilic-i].usilic\*[usilic-ie]/\*[usilic-i]usilicrc\*[usilic-ie] 00030/00062 48% 23107 usilic-1.5b
